{# Dual logging protocol - Council vs Scribe #}

### Session Start (MANDATORY)

Before any work, activate your Scribe project context once:
```python
# 1. Set project once (orchestrator provides name + root)
set_project(agent="<you>", name="<project>", root="<repo_root>")

# 2. Rehydrate — see what's happened so far
read_recent(agent="<you>", limit=5)
```

Do not repeat `set_project` before normal `append_entry` calls. Re-run it only when the project intentionally changes, or when an `append_entry`/Scribe response indicates sentinel/fallback/base-project mode or a project mismatch that needs correction.

### Council Logs (Milestones & Presence)

Use for: Session lifecycle, significant decisions, cross-agent events

```python
# Announce presence
log_audit(summary="Starting: auth system refactor", metadata={"phase": "init"})

# Log milestone
log_audit(summary="Phase 1 complete: all tests passing", metadata={"phase": "complete"})

# Store learning
store_memory(text="This codebase uses factory pattern for services", tags="pattern,architecture")
```

### Scribe Logs (Detailed Work Trail)

Use for: Every action, investigation step, code change, test result. Include reasoning traces.

```python
# Investigation (with reasoning)
append_entry(agent="<you>", message="Reading auth.py to understand current flow", status="info",
    meta={"reasoning": {"why": "Need to understand auth before refactoring", "what": "JWT flow", "how": "scan_only then line_range"}})

# Finding
append_entry(agent="<you>", message="Found bug: JWT expiry not checked", status="bug",
    meta={"file": "auth.py:142", "reasoning": {"why": "Security gap", "what": "No expiry validation", "how": "read_file scan_only revealed missing check"}})

# Change
append_entry(agent="<you>", message="Fixed JWT validation with 15min grace", status="success", meta={"files": 2})
```

### Scribe Documents (via manage_docs ONLY)

All documents under `.scribe/docs/dev_plans/` MUST use `manage_docs`:
```python
# Create research doc
manage_docs(agent="<you>", action="create", doc_name="RESEARCH_AUTH_20260130",
    metadata={"doc_type": "research", "research_goal": "Analyze auth flow"})

# Edit a section
manage_docs(agent="<you>", action="replace_section", doc_name="architecture",
    section="overview", content="## Overview\nUpdated content...")

# Update checklist
manage_docs(agent="<you>", action="status_update", doc_name="checklist",
    section="task_1", metadata={"status": "done", "proof": "All tests passing"})
```

### File Reading (prefer Scribe tools)

```python
# ALWAYS start with scan_only for structure
read_file(agent="<you>", path="src/module.py", mode="scan_only")

# Then targeted reads
read_file(agent="<you>", path="src/module.py", mode="line_range", start_line=100, end_line=150)

# Multi-file search
search(agent="<you>", pattern="class.*Handler", glob="**/*.py", output_mode="files_with_matches")
```

### When to Use Which

| Event | Council | Scribe |
|-------|---------|--------|
| Starting work | log_audit | set_project once + read_recent + append_entry |
| Reading a file | — | append_entry (prefer read_file over native Read) |
| Found a bug | store_memory | append_entry + open_bug |
| Made a decision | store_memory | append_entry |
| Created document | — | manage_docs + append_entry |
| Phase complete | log_audit | append_entry |
| Session end | end_session | — |
